.TH MCP-SERVER-GRAPHITI 1 "November 2026" "mcp-server-graphiti 1.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-server-graphiti \- MCP server for temporal Graphiti knowledge graphs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-server-graphiti
.RB [\|\-\-help \| \|\-\-version \|]
.RB [\|\-\-transport\ stdio|http|sse \|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-server-graphiti
exposes Graphiti episodic memory, entity search, fact search, provenance,
saga summaries and graph community operations through the Model Context
Protocol. The packaged configuration uses stdio and Neo4j.
.PP
External Graphiti services are initialized lazily when a tool is called.
MCP clients can therefore inspect the available tools before Neo4j or
OpenAI credentials are configured.
.SH READ-ONLY MODE
Set
.B MCP_SERVER_GRAPHITI_READ_ONLY=true
to register only non-mutating tools. The mcprack companion package sets this
by default.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/mcp-server-graphiti/config.yaml
.br
.I /usr/share/mcp-server-graphiti/server.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcprack (1)
